    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Mark Gonzalez represents the 54th District in the California State Assembly and is the Assembly Majority Whip. Elected in 2024, he previously chaired the Los Angeles County Democratic Party. He served as district director for former Assemblymember Miguel Santiago.",
        "cites": [1, 2],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Mark Gonzalez represents the 54th District in the California State Assembly and is the Assembly Majority Whip.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "Elected in 2024, he previously chaired the Los Angeles County Democratic Party.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "He served as district director for former Assemblymember Miguel Santiago.",
            "cites": [2]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "He introduced AB 1540 to reestablish the 988 LGBTQ+ youth suicide crisis line. He authored a bill to ban former federal immigration agents from state and local government jobs. He proposed AB 817 to require cold storage facilities to keep disaster contingency funds and make related settlements tax-free. He says he organized to pass a $25 hourly minimum wage for healthcare workers and an amendment protecting abortion rights. In one legislative session, he introduced 42 bills and 25 passed.",
        "cites": [3, 4, 5, 1, 2],
